  "name": "MojoAuth",
  "abstract": "Passwordless authentication service from the USA for consumer apps, behind a single API and hosted login page. It covers email OTP, magic links, SMS and WhatsApp OTP, passkeys (FIDO2/WebAuthn), authenticator-app OTP, One Tap and social login with any OpenID Connect provider, plus MFA, webhooks and a custom domain. Applications can use MojoAuth as an OpenID Provider (authorization code with PKCE) or as a SAML 2.0 identity provider, and enterprise SSO guides exist for Okta, Entra ID, Google Workspace and others. SDKs cover web frameworks, iOS, Android, Node.js, Go, .NET, Java and PHP. The Free plan covers 25,000 monthly active users, Business Pro scales by MAU, and Enterprise runs on a private cloud with RBAC, adaptive MFA and a 99.99% SLA.",
